# Shopping-bag delivery proposal r01

This is a concrete, unaccepted production-integration proposal for `shopping-bag.goods-carrier.n`. The candidate image and revised brief already have independent scoped visual acceptance. This directory adds no production media, entry changes, source rows, module readiness or new acceptance.

The exact accepted PNG is copied under `media/`; it has SHA256 `f978a606233240f896d7255e8f1454df0207194b207d88ef9d5502146c4558bb`, measures 414 by 512, and costs 135,843 encoded bytes and 1,695,744 conservatively accounted decoded bytes. The original source and all fifteen native comparison states were inspected before this proposal. The candidate probe's 534 checks and the independent visual decision remain historical candidate evidence. They will not be replayed.

## Reviewable changes

- `image-descriptor.proposed.json` is the exact proposed image descriptor.
- `entry-preimage.json`, `entry-afterimage.proposed.json` and `patch.proposed.json` show the complete single-entry before/after, the exact three note replacements and the protected projection. JSON-object hashes use `SHA256(JSON.stringify(value))`; file pins hash the exact file bytes.
- `resource.json` contains the exact content-addressed raw-media metadata. It is an individual resource proposal, not a new module manifest.
- `evidence-lock.json` pins twenty-one immutable source/acquisition/candidate/acceptance evidence files. Historical pending or false gates are preserved.
- `protected-media-observation.json` records the existing eight image and twelve audio descriptors and bytes. It is a narrow media observation, not a final shared registry baseline.
- `production-provenance-template.json` and `production-document-template.md` define the later durable provenance and documentation. They remain explicitly unintegrated templates.
- `integration-plan.md`, `test-delta-plan.md` and `rebase-contract.json` specify the bounded final rebase, installation and fresh persisted verification.

The proposed after-entry JSON hash is `25300b5f9d78a6327c16c27143f1aeddd9dba1c41bdd4e42c20f30d36148cc85`. The protected projection removes only `media.image` and `editorial_notes`; its unchanged JSON hash is `091cb33bb94c158215dc8db8c4198482b0c2f991ce4b964786321d5114c51d69`. Every remaining field is exact, including the user-approved Ava recording and reviewed morphology.

## Acceptance boundary

The image is a generic open carrier with a tall solid body and paired loop handles. It remains distinguishable from the accepted squat slotted shopping basket at the reviewed component sizes. An empty gift bag can share this shape, so the picture does not independently prove shopping use. The exact broad definition and accepted forms stay unchanged. The original fabric/flexibility/visible-purchases brief and its mismatch remain in retained evidence.

The existing `match`, `memory`, `pop`, `jelly` and `word_jelly` declarations remain exact. Retaining them does not grant new isolated-picture recognition, participant, responsive full-board, browser or whole-game acceptance. No `phrase` eligibility, narrower material meaning, `carrier bag` answer or new confusable ID is added. Current module readiness gates continue to apply.

## Work remaining before installation

Root must independently review this proposal, then bind a fresh small rebase to the actual successful fourth-ten committed and persisted-validation receipts. Shared source, registry and test hashes are deliberately absent here because fourth-ten preparation is still active. The rebase must preserve its eventual accepted changes, detect any shopping-bag preimage drift, and produce exact shared-test afterimages for independent review. Install only through the normal guarded transaction after those checks.

`author-proposal.cjs` was run once to author these local proposal files and perform generation sanity checks. It has exclusive-create outputs and is not a replay command. No test suite, engine, browser, build, production transaction or audio playback was dispatched by this task.
